# Input for the first part of `make test` (shell mode: "HEXVIEW.PRG /BIG.BIN").
# Time 0 = the program was started. The window opens at (8, 28): its content starts at
# screen (9, 44); the box's inside at (10, 45); the scroll bar at screen x 610-623.
# 1. the start of BIG.BIN: the 256 byte values, then text
1200 shot
# 2. PgDn twice (two pages), then Up three times (the lines move down: a copy back)
+200 {pgdn}{pgdn}
+300 {up}{up}{up}
+500 shot
# 3. End: the last page, "-- 64 KB here --" on the last line (offset 00FFF0)
+200 {end}
+500 shot
# 4. View > Go to offset... (ctrl+G): the dialog suggests the offset shown (selected)
+300 ^G
+800 shot
# typing replaces it: 1F0 and Enter (line 1F hex = 31 at the top)
+200 1f0\n
+600 shot
# 5. the mouse wheel over the box (3 lines a notch; -2 = two notches down), then the
# scroll bar's down arrow twice (screen 610-623, 285-298): 8 lines on, top 000270
+200 move 300 200
+200 wheel -2
+300 move 616 292
+200 click
+200 click
+500 shot
# 6. resize: drag the size grip (bottom right of the window, screen 630, 332) up and left;
# the box gets fewer lines and columns, the scroll bar and the status line move
+300 move 630 332
+200 press
+100 drag 480 240
+1000 release
+800 shot
# 7. and bigger again: more lines than at the start
+300 move 476 236
+200 press
+100 drag 634 352
+1000 release
+800 shot
# 8. Home, then close with ctrl+W (the kernel sends WE_CLOSE): the program ends
+200 {home}
+400 shot
+300 ^W
+800 shot
